{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1228856-hacks-alternate-feeding-requirements","id":1228856,"title":"Hacks - Alternate Feeding Requirements","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-06-20T07:59:31-07:00","id":1228856,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon3.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Hacks - Alternate Feeding Requirements","content":"So, this a variant on the Feeding/Blood restrictions for vampires. Feel free to add variations, critique, or come up with other hacks. <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\" style=\"width: 500px\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><b>Blood Potency</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><b>Feeding Requirements</b></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">1</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Any Blood</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">2</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Animal Blood</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">3</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Human Blood</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">4</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Recent Human Blood</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">5</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Fresh Human Blood</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">6</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Minor Ban/Requirement</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">7</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Moderate Ban</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">8</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Major Ban</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">9</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Severe Ban</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">10</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Pure Vitae</td> </tr> </table></div> The idea here is that vampires have more and more specific requirements on what they can drink, just like in core. But rather than a Animal/Human/Kindred delineation, this progresses at each stage of Blood Potency. Blood that qualifies at higher stages is always acceptable, of course.<br /> <br /> Any blood means that even synthetic blood would be acceptable.<br /> Animal and Human blood are self-explanatory.<br /> Recent means it has to be no more than 1 hour old (so stored blood).<br /> Fresh means it has to come straight from the circulatory system (no spilling blood into a container any more).<br /> Ban/Requirement means that the human has to fit some criteria like with some Bloodlines (such as infected blood for the Morbus). This starts out fairly broad, but gets increasingly specific, similar to how Ephemeral Bans do (which is why I reference the term). This makes Elders increasingly idiosyncratic as regarding their feeding preferences.<br /> Since Vitae is at the top of the list, it is always fair game. So Elders can still prey upon Neonates/other Vampires to get their fix if they can't find human with the right qualities.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 06-20-2018, 11:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-20T09:51:19-07:00","id":1228880,"title":"","content":"It's a good idea, but the Bans on BP 6-9 needs guidelines. The Bans of ephemeral entities works despite incredible vagueness because they're for NPCs. For player characters there should be some sort of structure to base it on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-20T10:17:19-07:00","id":1228887,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1228856-hacks-alternate-feeding-requirements?p=1228880#post1228880\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a good idea, but the Bans on BP 6-9 needs guidelines. The Bans of ephemeral entities works despite incredible vagueness because they're for NPCs. For player characters there should be some sort of structure to base it on.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's true. They do need guidelines. I'm just not sure what <i>exactly</i> those would be at the moment. For Minor, I was thinking something like &quot;A broad section of the population&quot; - Men, the Elderly, Brown-eyed, Virgins, etc. Not really a limiter, but still one. With it getting even more specific from there.<br /> <br /> It should be based on the character's traits, either something specific to their personality, history, Clan, etc. Like Banes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-20T15:06:17-07:00","id":1228977,"title":"","content":"Just shooting some ideas:<br /> <br /> 1. Any Blood<br /> 2. Any Animal Blood<br /> 3. Any Human Blood<br /> 4. Warm Human Blood (e.g. blood straight from the human body)<br /> 5. High-Quality Human Blood (e.g. healthy humans of good social standing)<br /> 6. Specific High-Quality Human Blood (e.g. healthy humans of good social standing with a specific trait, such as a specific hair color, eye color or race)<br /> 7. Any Kindred Blood<br /> 8. Blood Potency 3 Kindred Blood<br /> 9. Blood Potency 5 Kindred Blood<br /> 10. Bood Potency 7 Kindred Blood","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24044,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","user":"Ventrue Life","date":". 06-20-2018, 06:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-20T15:27:37-07:00","id":1228983,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ventrue Life</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1228856-hacks-alternate-feeding-requirements?p=1228977#post1228977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">5. High-Quality Human Blood (e.g. healthy humans of good social standing)<br /> 6. Specific High-Quality Human Blood (e.g. healthy humans of good social standing with a specific trait, such as a specific hair color, eye color or race)</div> </div> </div> </div>These seem like a bad idea, unless you specifically want to imply that social status has spiritual significance or wish to tie Kindred metaphysics to social status.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-20T15:48:43-07:00","id":1228988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1228856-hacks-alternate-feeding-requirements?p=1228983#post1228983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> These seem like a bad idea, unless you specifically want to imply that social status has spiritual significance or wish to tie Kindred metaphysics to social status.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's exactly what I'm implying. It's something that I remembered from Vampire The Masquerade - Bloodlines. The better a human does in life and the healthier he is, the higher quality their Vitae. At BP 5 and 6, you want to go after &quot;blue bloods&quot; so to speak. It might tie in to something mystical, or it might tie in to the simple fact that it makes sense that an actor or atlete with a professinal dietitian and personal health coach almost certainly has healthier more potent blood than a poor homeless person.<br /> <br /> See it as an expansion of the 'Distinguished Palate' Merit, because that's what I also based it on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-20T16:17:39-07:00","id":1229001,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ventrue Life</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1228856-hacks-alternate-feeding-requirements?p=1228988#post1228988\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See it as an expansion of the 'Distinguished Palate' Merit, because that's what I also based it on.</div> </div> </div> </div>Distinguished Palate can run off of something as value-neutral as hair-color or recent drug use. It's &quot;your character's Kindred sense of taste is discerning enough that they don't need a lucky roll to get huge amounts of detail from blood, but as a result they have a favored food and anything else doesn't give them the baseline returns.&quot;<br /> <br /> A character's health has no impact on the amount of Vitae a vampire takes from them to deal a point of damage \u2014 two turns of feeding on a frail junkie gives a vampire exactly as much sustenance as two turns of feeding on a teetotaling triathlete \u2014 and there are entire bloodlines built around feeding from &quot;unclean&quot; sources; the Morbus aren't locked out of Discerning Palate from their eating habits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-20T16:30:48-07:00","id":1229004,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1228856-hacks-alternate-feeding-requirements?p=1229001#post1229001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Distinguished Palate can run off of something as value-neutral as hair-color or recent drug use. It's &quot;your character's Kindred sense of taste is discerning enough that they don't need a lucky roll to get huge amounts of detail from blood, but as a result they have a favored food and anything else doesn't give them the baseline returns.&quot;<br /> <br /> A character's health has no impact on the amount of Vitae a vampire takes from them to deal a point of damage \u2014 two turns of feeding on a frail junkie gives a vampire exactly as much sustenance as two turns of feeding on a teetotaling triathlete \u2014 and there are entire bloodlines built around feeding from &quot;unclean&quot; sources; the Morbus aren't locked out of Discerning Palate from their eating habits.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> We're not talking about the rules as-is, but about alternate homebrew rules and ideas. I literally said &quot;Just shooting some ideas&quot; at the very start of my post. I thought that was pretty obvious, so I don't really understand why you're going over the existing rules and mechanics as a &quot;rebuttal&quot; to my idea, which is just an idea. I explained my idea as being in the same vein as 'Distinguished Palette', which also restricts your feeding to a specific trait, such as hair color or eye color and seems to suggest that arbitrary traits such as eye color and hair color can somehow affect how your blood tastes to a vampire. I don't see how social status as a limiting factor is any different from that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24044,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","user":"Ventrue Life","date":". 06-20-2018, 07:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-20T16:38:49-07:00","id":1229009,"title":"","content":"Distinguished Palate only applies to those who have the Merit, and, as mentioned, isn't exclusively tied to only one category. Your suggestion irrevocably ties a single characteristic to the metaphysics of all Kindred, which is a whole other can of worms and can bring a whole bunch of unfortunate implications, just like it did in VTMB. It's better to relegate such things to Merits or Bloodlines, where it only applies to the individual Kindred's or Bloodline's metaphysics.<br /> <br /> Tying it to the character's health could work, though. Making it more difficult to gain Vitae from the sickly would imply (or strengthen the already present implication) that Kindred drains health alongside blood from their victims. It gives Vitae a little more definition. I just recommend not tying it to mental health or anything like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-20T16:46:00-07:00","id":1229011,"title":"","content":"I wasn't talking about mental health in the first place. But there ya go then, change &quot;good social standing&quot; to &quot;healthy and properly nourished&quot; if that makes you feel better. That's basically what I was aiming at anyway, I just wanted it to keep it more vague so people can fill it in for themselves, In other words, you decide what &quot;good social standing&quot; means in your game or for your vampire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-23T17:17:15-07:00","id":1229679,"title":"","content":"Allowing synthetic blood at any level seems like a bad idea, but especially at BP 1. It rather undermines the personal horror of suddenly being a blood-sucking monster when that blood is just lab grown and ecologically friendly. You're basically a devoted vegan at that point. Wooo, the horror.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-23T18:14:32-07:00","id":1229693,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Unahim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1228856-hacks-alternate-feeding-requirements?p=1229679#post1229679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Allowing synthetic blood at any level seems like a bad idea, but especially at BP 1. It rather undermines the personal horror of suddenly being a blood-sucking monster when that blood is just lab grown and ecologically friendly. You're basically a devoted vegan at that point. Wooo, the horror.</div> </div> </div> </div>Have you thought about the practical concerns? The amount of synthetic blood required to be a &quot;devoted vegan&quot; can't really be sustainable for individuals who are psychologically (and practically, with sunlight) cut off from human society.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-23T18:35:30-07:00","id":1229696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1228856-hacks-alternate-feeding-requirements?p=1229693#post1229693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Have you thought about the practical concerns? The amount of synthetic blood required to be a &quot;devoted vegan&quot; can't really be sustainable for individuals who are psychologically (and practically, with sunlight) cut off from human society.</div> </div> </div> </div>Furthermore, this is only a recent possibility. only available in developed regions, and is expensive (as pointed out). It pretty much isn't an option for most newly Embraced vampires anyways, <i>and</i> will only last 50 years at most before they need better options.<br /> <br /> Further, you are <i>still</i> a blood-drinking corpse-person prone to rages and spontaneous combustion in the sunlight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-24T06:09:59-07:00","id":1229792,"title":"","content":"I think vampires (Requiem vampires at least) should have to do harm to feed, so synthetic blood feels wrong. Maybe...<br /> <br /> 1-2: Animals.<br /> <br /> 3-4: Mammals or stored human blood.<br /> <br /> 5-6: Human blood from the vein.<br /> <br /> 7-8: Vampire-tainted human blood from the vein (ghouls, dhampirs, someone a vampire has fed on before).<br /> <br /> 9-10: Vampires (could include revenants).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-24T07:01:42-07:00","id":1229796,"title":"","content":"Synthetic blood could work just not make it very economical<br /> <br /> <br /> Vampires who try to minimalize the harm they do, shouldnt be told &quot;thats imposxsibnle do something else&quot;<br /> <br /> though, I'd still agree <b>minimalize </b>not erradicate.<br /> <br /> The Scarred condition never goes away unless you injure someone.<br /> <br /> The swooning condition has implications of lust.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image